# 07: the KIT page. The SOURCE column (BUILT IN / SYNTH / SAMPLE) and a lane's EDIT.
title THE KIT
about The drum track's kit while the song plays: SOURCE says where each lane's sound comes from, built in, a drum synth or a recording, and EDIT cuts, turns round and pitches a lane's sound.
caption KIT
run --demo --view kit-source --samples $SAMPLES
from 0.6
length 24.0

0.8 say The kit: one row a lane.
2.4 say SOURCE. Hold A, down: SYNTH.
2.4 hold A 1.2
2.9 tap DOWN
4.4 say Hold A, up: BUILT IN, then SAMPLE.
4.4 hold A 2.0
4.9 tap UP 2 0.8
7.0 tap DOWN
7.6 tap A
9.0 say A on the picture: EDIT.
9.0 tap RIGHT
9.6 tap A
10.6 tap RIGHT
11.2 say Hold A on END: shorter.
11.2 hold A 1.4
11.6 stick DOWN 0.35
13.0 tap DOWN
13.4 say PITCH: three down.
13.4 hold A 1.6
13.8 tap DOWN 3 0.35
15.4 tap RIGHT 2 0.3
16.2 say REVERSE: end first.
16.2 hold A 1.0
16.6 tap UP
17.6 say Hold X: hear it. The file is not changed.
17.6 hold X 2.6
20.8 say B: the box back. B again: the kit.
21.2 tap B
22.0 tap B
